Article 4: Project Workflow and Execution
4.1 Client Onboarding Process
6. 	Sales team identifies potential clients through outreach, referrals, or website inquiries
7. 	Initial consultation is conducted to understand client requirements and project scope
8. 	Sales team prepares and presents a proposal with timeline and pricing
9. 	Upon client agreement, a formal contract is signed and initial payment is collected
10. Project details are handed over to the respective department co-founder
4.2 Project Assignment and Execution
11. Sales team creates a detailed project brief including requirements, deadlines, and client expectations
12. The brief is shared with the appropriate department co-founder based on service type
◦        Web development projects go to the CTO
◦        Mechanical design projects go to the Head of Engineering
◦        Design and branding projects go to the Design Head
◦        Marketing projects are coordinated between Sales team and Director of Growth
13. The department co-founder assigns the project to a team member or works on it personally
14. Team member executes the project according to specifications and best practices
15. Regular updates are shared with the department co-founder and sales team
4.3 Quality Review and Approval
16. Once work is completed, the team member prepares a comprehensive project document
17. The document must include deliverables, source files, documentation, and any relevant notes
18. The respective department co-founder conducts a thorough review and testing
◦        Checks for quality, accuracy, and compliance with client requirements
◦        Tests functionality and user experience where applicable
◦        Reviews all documentation for completeness
19. If revisions are needed, the co-founder provides detailed feedback and returns to the team
20. Once approved, the co-founder forwards the deliverable to the sales team
21. The CEO may conduct a final review before client submission for high-value projects


4.4 Client Delivery and Follow-up
22. Sales team receives the approved deliverable from the department co-founder
23. Sales team prepares client presentation and handover materials
24. Deliverable is submitted to the client with proper documentation and instructions
25. Sales team collects client feedback and final payment
26. Any revision requests are routed back through the department co-founder
27. Project is marked as complete and archived for future reference
Article 5: Financial Management
5.1 Financial Authority
•        All financial matters are managed by the CEO (Harsh Srivastava)
•        The CEO has the authority to appoint finance team members for tracking and reporting
•        All major financial decisions require CEO approval
•        Budget allocation is determined by the CEO in consultation with co-founders
5.2 Payment Collection and Processing
•        All client payments are collected by the sales team
•        Initial deposits must be received before project work begins
•        Final payments must be collected before final deliverable handover
•        All payments are recorded in the company financial system within 24 hours
5.3 Expense Management
•        Department co-founders can approve operational expenses up to a pre-defined limit
•        Expenses above the limit require CEO approval
•        All expenses must be properly documented with receipts and purpose
•        Monthly expense reports are submitted to the CEO by each department
5.4 Salary and Compensation
•        All team members receive compensation on a fixed schedule
•        Salary decisions are made by the CEO with input from department co-founders
•        Performance bonuses may be awarded for exceptional work
Article 6: Communication and Collaboration
6.1 Internal Communication Channels
•        All team communication happens through approved company channels
•        Project updates must be shared regularly with relevant stakeholders
•        Department co-founders meet weekly to discuss ongoing projects and challenges
•        Emergency issues should be escalated immediately to the relevant co-founder
6.2 Client Communication
•        All client communication is managed through the sales team
•        Team members should not contact clients directly unless authorized
•        Client feedback is collected by sales and shared with the respective department
•        Professional and timely responses are mandatory for all client inquiries
6.3 Documentation Standards
•        All projects must be properly documented from start to finish
•        Code, designs, and technical work should include clear comments and explanations
•        Project files are stored in the company repository for future reference
Article 7: Quality Standards and Best Practices
7.1 Quality Commitment
•        All work must meet professional industry standards
•        No deliverable goes to a client without co-founder approval
•        Quality issues discovered after delivery must be fixed immediately at no extra cost
•        Team members are expected to continuously improve their skills and knowledge
7.2 Human-First Approach
•        All deliverables must feel human and personalized, not generic or automated
•        While AI tools can assist in work, final outputs must be reviewed and refined by humans
•        Copy, design, and code should reflect understanding of the client's unique needs
•        Team members should add their personal expertise and creativity to every project
7.3 Testing and Validation
•        All technology projects must be tested across different devices and browsers
•        Mechanical designs must be validated for manufacturability and functionality
•        Design work must be reviewed for brand consistency and visual appeal

Article 8: Team Management and Development
8.1 Hiring and Onboarding
•        Department co-founders have authority to hire team members for their departments
•        All new hires must be approved by the CEO before finalizing the offer
•        New team members receive proper onboarding and training
•        Company culture, values, and workflows are explained during onboarding
8.2 Performance Management
•        Regular performance reviews are conducted by department co-founders
•        Feedback should be constructive and focused on growth
•        Underperforming team members receive support and improvement plans
•        Persistent performance issues may result in termination
8.3 Professional Development
•        Team members are encouraged to learn new skills and technologies
•        The company supports training and certification programs where appropriate
•        Knowledge sharing sessions are held regularly within departments
Article 9: Operational Rules and Policies
9.1 Working Hours and Availability
•        Standard working hours are defined by each department co-founder
•        Team members must be available during agreed working hours
•        Flexible arrangements can be made for valid reasons with co-founder approval
•        Urgent client matters may require work outside normal hours
9.2 Project Deadlines
•        All project deadlines must be honored unless circumstances prevent it
•        If a delay is anticipated, the team member must notify the co-founder immediately
•        The co-founder will inform the sales team, who will manage client expectations
•        Repeated missed deadlines will result in performance review
9.3 Confidentiality and Data Security
•        All client information and project details are strictly confidential
•        Team members must not share proprietary information outside the company
•        Project files must be stored securely in company-approved systems
•        Data breaches or security violations must be reported immediately
9.4 Professional Conduct
•        All team members must maintain professional behavior at all times
•        Respectful communication is required with clients and colleagues
•        Conflicts should be resolved professionally through proper channels
•        Harassment, discrimination, or unprofessional behavior will not be tolerated
9.5 Leave and Absence
•        Team members must request time off in advance from their department co-founder
•        Leave requests should consider project deadlines and team workload
•        Emergency leave can be granted with proper notification
•        Excessive or unplanned absences may affect performance evaluations
Article 10: Decision Making and Governance
10.1 Authority Levels
•        Team members have authority over their assigned tasks and daily work decisions
•        Department co-founders have authority over departmental decisions and project approvals
•        The CEO has final authority on company-wide decisions, finances, and strategic direction
•        Major decisions affecting the entire company require input from all co-founders
10.2 Conflict Resolution
•        Disagreements between team members should first be resolved directly
•        If resolution fails, the matter is escalated to the department co-founder
•        Conflicts between co-founders are mediated by the CEO
•        All parties must approach conflicts professionally and in good faith
10.3 Policy Changes
•        This constitution may be amended with agreement from all co-founders
•        Proposed changes should be discussed in a formal co-founder meeting
•        All team members will be notified of any policy updates
•        Changes take effect from the date specified by the leadership team


Article 11: Client Service Excellence
11.1 Client Satisfaction
•        Client satisfaction is the top priority for every project
•        Feedback from clients should be taken seriously and acted upon
•        Revisions requested by clients should be completed promptly
•        Long-term client relationships are valued and nurtured
11.2 Project Support
•        Post-delivery support is provided as specified in the project contract
•        Bug fixes and minor adjustments are handled quickly
•        Additional services beyond the original scope require a new agreement
11.3 Portfolio and Case Studies
•        Completed projects may be featured in the company portfolio with client permission
•        Client testimonials are collected for marketing purposes
•        Confidential projects are not shared publicly without explicit consent
Article 12: Growth and Innovation
12.1 Continuous Improvement
•        The company encourages innovation and new ideas from all team members
•        Processes and workflows should be regularly reviewed for efficiency
•        New tools and technologies are evaluated for potential adoption
12.2 Service Expansion
•        New service offerings are considered based on market demand and team capabilities
•        Service additions require approval from all co-founders
•        Proper training and resources are allocated before launching new services
12.3 Market Positioning
•        The company maintains a strong online presence through website and social media
•        Marketing efforts focus on showcasing expertise and successful projects
•        Brand reputation is protected through quality work and professional conduct
 
